content.text:
Landscape is definitely broken: the stage is only 136px tall, marquee overlaps stage UI, machine tiny. The requirement: "Responsive desktop/mobile layout with usable touch controls." Landscape phones are mobile. We should improve landscape.

Options:
- At landscape short heights (max-height: 520px) and width ≤980, switch topbar to single row with brand + tabs + wallet? Could reduce topbar height. But stage still limited: total 390 - padding 16 - topbar (say 50) - dock (100) - gaps = ~210. Better than 136 but still small. Could also compact the dock in landscape: put denom strip and action in one row? Or reduce dock height by hiding the claw/denom strip? Denom strip is needed. Could make dock two columns: denom strip left, action right, meta hidden. Height ~70. Then stage ~250. Still small but playable-ish.

Alternative: in landscape, use the sidebar? No width 844, can't fit.

Could overlay the control dock on the stage bottom as a floating panel, giving stage nearly full height? E.g., in short landscape, hide topbar tabs row? Let's design:

@media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape) {
  .app { padding: 4px 8px; gap: 4px; }
  .topbar { grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; grid-template-areas: "brand tabs wallet"; min-height: 40px; gap: 8px; }
  .brand h1 { font-size: 15px; }
  .brand-emblem { width: 30px; height: 30px; flex-basis: 30px; }
  .brand-kicker, .brand-sub { display: none; }
  .mode-tabs { ... height 38px }
  .mode-tab { min-height: 34px; padding: 2px 8px; }
  .tab-icon { display: none; } // save width
  .wallet { min-height: 34px; }
  .wallet-coin { width: 24px; height: 24px; }
  .wallet strong { font-size: 15px; }
  .wallet-label { display: none; }
  .icon-btn { width: 32px; height: 32px; }
  .main { ... }
  .control-dock { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 4px 8px; }
  .denom-strip { flex: 1; height: 32px; padding: 0; border-bottom: 0; }
  .claw-strip { flex: 1; height: 32px; padding: 0; border-bottom: 0; }
  .dock-main { padding-top: 0; flex: 0 0 auto; gap: 8px; }
  .dock-copy, .dock-meta { display: none; }
  .primary-action { width: 170px; flex-basis: 170px; height: 44px; }
  .stage { border-radius: 14px; }
  .stage-ui--top { top: 6px; left: 8px; right: 8px; }
  .stage-ui--bottom { display: none? } // to save visual clutter
  .hint { bottom: 8px; ... } // might overlap machine, but stage taller now
  .toast-stack { top: ... dynamic }
}

But the canvas layout computes based on stage height. With stage ~270px, pusher machine renders small but okay. Claw case h = min(0.63*270=170, 530), caseTop=54, bottom=224, base 54 → 278 > stage 270, clipped slightly. The claw base may overflow. But the canvas clips at stage; machine base bottom slightly cut. Could adjust computeClawLayout for short heights: caseH = min(h*0.63, 530) but for h=270, 0.63*270=170; base 54 + 12 → 236, stage 270, fine (54+170+12+54=290 > 270? caseTop=0.2*270=54; caseBottom=54+170=224; base y=236, h=max(54,28)=54 → bottom 290 > 270 by 20). So base clipped 20px. Could reduce base h for short: h = max(38, h*0.105). Then 38 → bottom 274, slight. Or caseH = min(h*0.6, 530). For 270: 162 → caseBottom=54+162=216, base y=228, h=38 → 266. Good. But modifying computeClawLayout affects all sizes; can add a condition for h < 360: caseH = min(h*0.58, 530), base min 38. Let's see.

However, is landscape support required? "Responsive desktop/mobile layout with usable touch controls." Mobile includes portrait primarily; landscape is common for games. The current landscape is not usable (stage 136px). Adding a short-landscape media query is worthwhile.

Let's implement a compact landscape layout. Need to be careful not to break other breakpoints.

Approach:
- Add `@media (max-height: 560px) and (orientation: landscape) and (max-width: 980px)` (or just max-height 560 & max-width 980) at the end of styles.css before reduced motion.
- Compact topbar to one row with grid areas brand tabs wallet. The topbar currently at ≤980 has two rows via grid-template-areas. Override.
- Reduce gaps/padding.
- Compact dock to single row: `.control-dock { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }` with denom strip flex, dock-main flex. But `.control-dock` children: denom-strip, claw-strip, dock-main. For pusher, denom strip + dock-main; for claw, claw strip + dock-main. `.dock-main` contains dock-copy (hidden on mobile already), action button, dock-meta. On mobile ≤980, dock-copy display none, action flex, meta 82px. For landscape, hide dock-meta and set action width 160. Set `.dock-main { padding-top: 0; flex: 0 0 auto; }`.
- `.denom-strip { flex: 1 1 auto; height: 34px; padding-bottom: 0; border-bottom: 0; }`.
- `.denom { height: 28px; }` already.
- `.claw-strip { flex: 1 1 auto; height: 34px; padding-bottom: 0; border-bottom: 0; justify-content: flex-start; }`.
- `.primary-action { width: 180px; flex-basis: 180px; height: 46px; }`.
- Topbar: `.topbar { grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0,1fr) auto; grid-template-areas: "brand tabs wallet"; min-height: 0; gap: 8px; }`. `.brand-emblem` 34px. `.brand h1` 16px. Hide brand-kicker/sub. `.mode-tabs { align-self: center; }` `.mode-tab { min-height: 36px; }` `.tab-icon { width: 24px; height:24px; flex-basis:24px; }` maybe hide to save space: `.tab-icon { display: none; }` and `.mode-tab { padding: 4px 10px; }`. `.tab-copy small { display: none; }` to reduce height? Keep b only. Mode tabs height ~36.
- Wallet compact: `.wallet { min-height: 36px; padding: 3px 8px 3px 4px; }`, `.wallet-coin { width: 26px; height: 26px; }`, `.wallet strong { font-size: 16px; }`, `.wallet-label { display: none; }`, `.icon-btn { width: 34px; height: 34px; }`.
- Stage UI bottom hide? Keep but small. `.stage-ui--bottom { display: none; }` to free visual space, but aim readout useful. Could keep at bottom 4px. With stage 250px, chips at bottom overlay the machine tray. Hmm. Keep but smaller; they already small at ≤560. Fine.
- Hint at bottom: with dock now beside, hint at bottom 8px? It would cover tray/base. At stage 250, hint 30px tall, bottom 8 → covers bottom 38px. That's the machine base. Fine. But it could overlap stage bottom chips at bottom 8. Hide bottom chips in landscape, or move hint bottom 34. Let's hide `.stage-ui--bottom` in landscape and set hint bottom: 10px. Toast dynamic top below marquee; marquee for pusher h=250: y=11.75, marqueeH=min(33.75,94)=33.75 → bottom 45.5; toast top 57.5. That's over the table. Fine.
- `.big-win { top: 42%; }`.
- `.app { padding: 4px 8px calc(4px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom)); gap: 4px; }`.

Height math at 844x390: padding top/bottom 4+4=8; topbar ~40; gap 4; main (stage+dock+gap 4). Available for main = 390-8-40-4 = 338. Dock ~46+8 padding? `.control-dock` padding 4px 8px → height ~46+8=54. Stage = 338-4-54=280. Better. Canvas claw: caseH=min(0.63*280=176,530)=176; caseTop=56; caseBottom=232; base y=244; h=max(54,29)=54 → 298 > 280 by 18. Need adjust computeClawLayout for short h. Add:
```
const compact = h < 360;
const caseH = Math.min(h * (compact ? 0.58 : 0.63), 530);
...
prizeBase: clamp(caseW * 0.065, 14, 56)
...
```
For h=280: caseTop=56, caseH=162.4 → caseBottom=218.4, base y=230.4, base h = max(compact?38:54, h*0.105=29.4) = 38 → 268.4 < 280. Good.
